Classic with a Twist
"Kill the thing… but it runs"
Target tries to flee to a safe zone → turns into an escort intercept mission.
Trigger trick: On unit health < 30%, change owner to neutral, give it insane speed, and enable new trigger for "if it reaches escape region".

"Go to the spot… but it's a trap"
Player reaches area → spawns ambush, new objective: survive or escape to new point.
Trigger trick: "Unit enters region" → spawn enemy wave, change objective text, start timer.

🔄 Dynamic & Reactive
"Steal the intel, but now they're hunting you"
Gather objective → triggers "hunted" mode where enemy patrols actively search for your hero.
Trigger trick: Set boolean Hunted = true, run periodic trigger that spawns search parties near player's hero if Hunted == true.

"Your choices change the battlefield"
Destroy bridge? Enemy takes longer route. Spare village? They send reinforcements later.
Trigger trick: Use integer variables like Village_Alive = 1. Later trigger checks: if Village_Alive == 1, spawn ally units at 15:00.

⏳ Time Pressure Layers
"Gather resources while the doom clock ticks"
Main objective: build superweapon in 20 minutes.
Secret speed-run bonus: if done in 10, enemy's final wave is half strength.
Trigger trick: Two victory conditions checking same objective but with different timers.

🎭 The Bait-and-Switch
"Defend this position… just kidding, fall back!"
After holding for 2 minutes, command comes: "Retreat now!" New objective: get your core units to extraction.
Trigger trick: Timer expires → display new objective, change music, create retreat waypoint.

💡 Trigger Pro-Tips for Your Engine
If you're rolling your own in something like Unity/C#, think in modular conditions:

csharp
// Simple objective tracker structure
public class Objective {
    public string description;
    public bool isCompleted;
    public System.Action onComplete;
    
    // Check conditions each frame
    public void Check() {
        if (/* condition met */) {
            isCompleted = true;
            onComplete?.Invoke();
        }
    }
}

// Chain them
Objective destroyEnemyBase = new Objective(...);
destroyEnemyBase.onComplete += () => {
    // Spawn next objective
    StartCoroutine(EscapeSequence());
};
🎯 Player Psychology Hacks
The "Almost Lost" – Let player's base get to 10% health, then trigger reinforcements.

The "False Victory" – Player completes objective, celebration starts… then bigger threat emerges.

The "Meaningful Choice" – Save villagers OR secure tech, each giving different late-game bonuses.

